ason": "Structural formula now correct: max_abs collapsed from c001's ~5e3 to ~20 (250x reduction) purely by switching to the exact sequential per-layer mask application, confirming (a) the mask is non-trivial random and (b) layer order matters. Remaining error is uniform (~17-22 max_abs) across ALL five WLs regardless of B*T, i.e. NOT a size-dependent tiling/boundary bug but a global precision gap. The random mask multiplies the work buffer every layer (values grow ~mask^k), and with rtol=1e-5 (200x below TF32's ~2e-3 relative error) large-magnitude elements exceed atol=0.01+rtol*|ref|, so >1% mismatch. Diagnosis: reference is effectively FP32; TF32 tl.dot cannot meet the gate. Next candidate c003 = same exact-sequential structure but FP32 accumulate (ALLOW_TF32=False) to close the precision gap.", "cumulative_evaluations": 2, "skill_usage": "KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools."}
