 "max_rel": 0.4229}], "all_passed": true, "geomean_speedup": 0.5026458432077623, "arithmetic_mean_speedup": 0.5718769580083973, "decision": "champion", "reason": "FIRST VALID candidate: 5/5 pass. Precision fix (TF32->FP32) closed the gate exactly as diagnosed - max_abs dropped from c002's ~20 to <=0.018 (all within atol=0.011+rtol*|ref| for >=99% of elements). Becomes standing champion. HOWEVER geomean=0.50x is a SLOWDOWN vs reference (cuDNN). Per-WL: WL1 0.88x, WL2 0.73x, WL4 0.58x, WL3 0.49x, WL5 0.17x. WL5 (B=64,T=8192, compute-bound) is the dominant drag: full-FP32 tl.dot lowers to FMA (no tensor cores) so we lose ~8x vs cuDNN TF32. Root tension: FP32 needed for correctness kills throughput on the big WL. Next levers to beat cuDNN while staying FP32-accurate: (a) reduce kernel/launch count and buffer round-trips (12 conv launches + 4 combine per call); (b) better tiling/num_warps/num_stages, esp. larger tiles + pipelining for WL5; (c) investigate a TF32+FP32-residual correction (3xTF32 / split-K) to reclaim tensor-core throughput while meeting rtol=1e-5. c004 will target tiling+fusion for WL5.", "cumulative_evaluations": 3, "skill_usage": "KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools."}
